# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data folders: keep the SKELETON, ignore the CONTENTS.
#
# conf/config.yaml hardcodes absolute paths into SegmentedForests/<...>, so a
# fresh clone must already have those directories or the stages fail on a
# missing folder. Git cannot track an empty directory, so each one holds a
# .gitkeep placeholder file.
#
# GOTCHA: ignore the contents (`SegmentedForests/**`), never the directory
# itself (`SegmentedForests/`). Git does not descend into an ignored directory,
# so a `!` re-include underneath one is silently dead. Comments must also sit on
# their own line -- a trailing `# ...` becomes part of the pattern.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SegmentedForests/**
# let git descend into the subfolders...
!SegmentedForests/**/
# ...so the placeholders that preserve the structure can be tracked
!SegmentedForests/**/.gitkeep

# Real inputs that belong in the repo: the per-plot 3DFin settings.
!SegmentedForests/3DFin_settings/*.ini

# Small Stage-2 metadata (shifts + source CRS/scales); the .ply/.las/.laz next
# to them stay ignored by the rule above.
!SegmentedForests/ForAINet_input/*_offsets.yml

# Class-unifier provenance sidecars (column names/dtypes, class_map, per-class
# counts) are a few KB and worth versioning -- the N x 7 .npy matrix beside them
# is ~1 GB and regenerable, so it stays ignored.
!SegmentedForests/ClassUnifier_output/*.json

# Per-run Hydra logs
outputs/

# Python / Jupyter cruft
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Offset file the misc converter writes next to itself
misc/offset.yml

# Working area for data pulled out of the repo (e.g. the old .ply training set)
temp_removed/

# Archived training dataset (~1 GB zip): kept on disk, never in git.
old_training_dataset/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ForAINet/ is a SUBMODULE -- nothing here applies inside it.
#
# A parent .gitignore never governs a submodule's contents; the submodule keeps
# its own index and ignore rules. (Two further reasons the old
# `ForAINet\PointCloudSegmentation\...` lines did nothing: .gitignore always
# uses forward slashes, and a backslash is an escape character, not a
# separator.) These paths also come from upstream's pinned commit, so ignoring
# them could not remove them anyway.
#
# To stop the submodule reporting its local data as untracked, exclude it from
# INSIDE the submodule -- local only, leaves upstream's tracked files alone:
#     ForAINet/.git/info/exclude
#
# To avoid having unused upstream subprojects (superpoint_graph/, tree_metrics/)
# on disk at all, use a sparse checkout rather than an ignore rule:
#     git -C ForAINet sparse-checkout set PointCloudSegmentation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
